# Grass
> Grass is a global network of residential data nodes powered by millions of people who contribute unused bandwidth to collect and organize the world's information to advance AI development.
> Get rewarded for the internet you don't use. Grass is a decentralized network of millions of people who earn rewards for sharing unused internet bandwidth; verified institutions use that bandwidth to turn public web data into structured datasets for AI and enterprise use.

Grass does not access your private information, browsing history, or files, and does not sell personal data. The Grass app runs quietly in the background on desktop, browser, and Android. Contribution is measured in Grass Points (Uptime Points and Network Points), which factor into Grass Token rewards. Token distributions and governance are run by the Grass Foundation. The full reference is in [/llms-full.txt](https://www.grass.io/llms-full.txt); AI usage and citation policy is in [/ai.txt](https://www.grass.io/ai.txt).

